# Naming-translation table for use with -rigidbody: it maps a bead's
# canonical label ("BB", "SC1") to the grain name the reduction gave it
# ("ABB", "ASC1"). Generated by data/martini3/prepare_martini3_data.py -- do
# not edit by hand.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. A grain name must be unique per residue, because the
# force-field key IS the grain name (ReduceRule::forcefield_key) and the
# backbone types differ by residue: GLY is SP1, ALA SP2, PRO SP2a, every
# other P2. So the reduction names alanine's backbone bead "ABB". But a
# .rbody rule has to say "+BB" to reach the NEXT residue's backbone, and it
# cannot know what that residue is, so it cannot say "+ABB".
#
# RigidBodyBuilder resolves exactly this: when an atom is not found under the
# name the .rbody wrote, it translates that name through a table, IN THE
# TARGET RESIDUE'S CONTEXT (RigidBodyBuilder::_translate takes
# target_resname). So "+BB" on an alanine followed by a glycine resolves to
# "GBB". The table it accepts must have EXACTLY ONE ATOM PER RULE --
# _check_translation_is_one_atom_per_rule kills pdb2spn otherwise -- which is
# why reducerules/martini3.grp cannot serve as the table and this file has to
# exist.
#
# It is therefore NOT a reduction. Passing it to a run that would reduce
# would destroy the model: the rule "ABB ALA BB" looks for an atom named BB,
# and an all-atom structure has none. Use it only with an input that is
# already coarse-grained, where pdb2spn skips the reduction -- see the
# two-step recipe in README.md.
#
ABB ALA BB
ASC1 ALA SC1
CBB CYS BB
CSC1 CYS SC1
DBB ASP BB
DSC1 ASP SC1
DHBB ASH BB
DHSC1 ASH SC1
EBB GLU BB
ESC1 GLU SC1
EHBB GLH BB
EHSC1 GLH SC1
FBB PHE BB
FSC1 PHE SC1
FSC2 PHE SC2
FSC3 PHE SC3
GBB GLY BB
HBB HIS BB
HSC1 HIS SC1
HSC2 HIS SC2
HSC3 HIS SC3
HEBB HIE BB
HESC1 HIE SC1
HESC2 HIE SC2
HESC3 HIE SC3
HPBB HIP BB
HPSC1 HIP SC1
HPSC2 HIP SC2
HPSC3 HIP SC3
IBB ILE BB
ISC1 ILE SC1
KBB LYS BB
KSC1 LYS SC1
KSC2 LYS SC2
KNBB LYN BB
KNSC1 LYN SC1
KNSC2 LYN SC2
LBB LEU BB
LSC1 LEU SC1
MBB MET BB
MSC1 MET SC1
NBB ASN BB
NSC1 ASN SC1
OBB HYP BB
OSC1 HYP SC1
PBB PRO BB
PSC1 PRO SC1
QBB GLN BB
QSC1 GLN SC1
RBB ARG BB
RSC1 ARG SC1
RSC2 ARG SC2
SBB SER BB
SSC1 SER SC1
TBB THR BB
TSC1 THR SC1
VBB VAL BB
VSC1 VAL SC1
WBB TRP BB
WSC1 TRP SC1
WSC2 TRP SC2
WSC3 TRP SC3
WSC4 TRP SC4
WSC5 TRP SC5
YBB TYR BB
YSC1 TYR SC1
YSC2 TYR SC2
YSC3 TYR SC3
YSC4 TYR SC4
